From a52f800a66f5e99689c1438e0c1257fff563dd08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): vectorize indexer KPool loads and co-schedule
 dense CTA columns

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
1. In indexer_score_v41, load_keys mapped T.Parallel(64, 128) across 128 threads with 2 E2M1 elements (1 byte) per thread along D=128 and a 32-iteration loop along block_P=64, and TileLang failed to vectorize across the conditional bounds check and 16-byte swizzle boundary. Each thread issued 32 scalar 1-byte LDG.E.U8 loads, 32 1-byte STS.U8 stores, and 33 redundant PageTable global loads per 64-position tile (1,223 SASS instructions / 148 registers on ptxas 13.0.88; 1,518 SASS instructions / 250 registers on ptxas 13.5.37). Replacing load_keys with 16-byte uint4 (32 E2M1) global loads, a single hoisted PageTable lookup per tile/row, and direct swizzled STS.128 stores reduces indexer_score_v41 to 528 SASS instructions (-56.8%) and 68 registers on 13.0.88 (535 SASS instructions and 67 registers on 13.5.37).
2. In multi-row dense scoring (rows > 1, e.g. MTP verification), launching (ctas, rows) as (bx, by) scheduled all 128 CTAs of row 0 in Waves 0..1 on GB10 before row 1..5 launched, streaming the entire KPool and evicting early tiles from the 24 MB L2 cache before rows 1..5 could reuse them. Mapping cta = (by * ctas + bx) // rows and row = (by * ctas + bx) % rows co-schedules all rows of each persistent CTA column in the same wave so rows 1..5 hit L2 on row 0's KPool loads, cutting cold-L2 6-row indexer_score_v41 latency by 38.5%-50.1% across 16K-262K context (481.3 -> 240.0 us at 262K, saving 241.7 us/layer or -37.3% across the full post-MoE attention block).

Quality:
Bit-identical outputs (torch.equal == True) across dense and candidate modes; preserves exact out-of-bounds read predicates verified under compute-sanitizer --tool initcheck.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_lsa.py (66 passed, 1 xfailed across 2 boots, including compute-sanitizer initcheck).

Upstream status: local SM120/SM121 TileLang indexer optimization.
